 ## Architecture at a glance
 
 - **Monorepo** — Turborepo. Apps: `backend` (NestJS 10 + Prisma 5 + PostgreSQL 16 + Redis 7; Bull queues, crons, and Socket.io all in the ONE backend process), `frontend` (Next.js 14 App Router, `[locale]` segment, Tailwind + shadcn/ui, React Query + Zustand + RHF/Zod). Packages: `shared-types`, `validators`, `constants`, `permissions` (the shared permission resolver + the typed key catalog — run by the backend AND the browser since W2).
-- **Single internal portal** at `apps/frontend/src/app/[locale]/admin/` — every authenticated user is staff; the only public surface is `/careers/*` + auth. Global chrome is the 3-column "Command" shell (`src/components/layout/command-*`), with all module nav declared as data in `src/config/modules.ts`.
+- **Single internal portal** at `apps/frontend/src/app/[locale]/admin/` — every authenticated user is staff; the public surfaces are `/careers/*`, auth, and the token-guarded machine doors — the İŞKUR/Indeed agent routes, the §7.8/§7.9 webhooks and, since WP3a, the website intake door `/api/website/v1/*` (PRD §7.10). Global chrome is the 3-column "Command" shell (`src/components/layout/command-*`), with all module nav declared as data in `src/config/modules.ts`.
 - **Auth** — JWT access (15 min) + refresh (30 d, Redis, rolling); optional TOTP 2FA. `REFRESH_TTL_SECONDS` (`auth.service.ts`) and frontend `COOKIE_MAX_AGE` (`stores/auth.store.ts`) must stay in lockstep.
-- **Permissions** — database-driven: 12 system roles × **75 grantable keys** (22 modules + 53 screen-level resources, all enforced) × 13 actions × 3 scopes, plus per-USER overrides; catalog served by `GET /api/permissions/catalog`. **One resolver answers everything** — `EffectivePermissionsService` — and the BROWSER runs that same resolver, from `@jobsadmire/permissions`, over the inputs `GET /permissions/me/effective` returns. Use `@RequirePermission('key','ACTION')` server-side and `<Can>`/`usePermissions()` client-side. CASL survives as a projection for nine service-layer call sites, not as the decision point. Super-admin bypasses via `can('manage','all')`. **No code decides access by comparing a role slug** — a repo invariant refuses a new one, and the few that remain are declared policies about whose ACCOUNT may be touched. The programme that built this ran W0–W4 on 2026-09-15; PRD §4 describes the result, §4.8 the engine internals, §4.9 the route manifest + page guard.
+- **Permissions** — database-driven: 12 system roles × **85 grantable keys** (23 modules + 62 screen-level resources, all enforced) × 13 actions × 3 scopes, plus per-USER overrides; catalog served by `GET /api/permissions/catalog`. **One resolver answers everything** — `EffectivePermissionsService` — and the BROWSER runs that same resolver, from `@jobsadmire/permissions`, over the inputs `GET /permissions/me/effective` returns. Use `@RequirePermission('key','ACTION')` server-side and `<Can>`/`usePermissions()` client-side. CASL survives as a projection for nine service-layer call sites, not as the decision point. Super-admin bypasses via `can('manage','all')`. **No code decides access by comparing a role slug** — a repo invariant refuses a new one, and the few that remain are declared policies about whose ACCOUNT may be touched. The programme that built this ran W0–W4 on 2026-09-15; PRD §4 describes the result, §4.8 the engine internals, §4.9 the route manifest + page guard.
 - **Storage** — MinIO in BOTH dev and prod (prod behind `files.operations.jobsadmire.com`). There is no S3.
 - **i18n** — next-intl, English + Turkish.
 - **Local dev** — Docker Compose (`npm run dev`), host ports 4xxx (CRM sibling owns 3xxx). Backend container self-runs `prisma generate / migrate deploy / db seed` on boot.
 - **Deploy** — a VPS **cron poller** auto-deploys `main` within ~2 min of a push (GitHub Actions is billing-suspended org-wide). Details, env inventory, runbooks: `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`.
 
