+**Alarms and retention (P10, RC6).** `WebsiteAbuseService` counts REAL, NON-REPLAYED, CAPTCHA-VERIFIED submissions per form in a 60-minute Redis window (`website:abuse:count:<form>` — `recordVerified` is called only when the outcome was `passed` (not `degraded`), the token class was not `test`, and the row was newly created, not a P2002 replay) and trips at `WEBSITE_ABUSE_TRIP_THRESHOLD = 25` (`website:abuse:tripped:<form>`, announced once via `website:abuse:announced:<form>`); a tripped form answers 429 with the WhatsApp-fallback hint; `ping.trippedForms` reads the same keys. The `website-alarms` cron (every 5 min) announces untrips and checks drought ONLY inside `WEBSITE_BUSINESS_HOURS` (Europe/Istanbul, Mon–Fri 09:00–18:00 — so a quiet Friday afternoon alarms Monday morning, not over the weekend). **`isLeadDrought` returns `false` when no real submission has EVER arrived (X14)** — a door that is merely new is indistinguishable from one that is broken, and alarming on every fresh deploy or a not-yet-launched form would be noise; only once a real (non-test) submission exists does silence for `WEBSITE_DROUGHT_HOURS = 48` raise `WEBSITE_FORMS_UNAVAILABLE(reason: drought)`, once per company day. The `website-purge` cron at **04:30** (container clock; 03:00 is `careers-retention`'s slot) runs two sweeps: the 90-day row purge (`purgeAfter`, post-HANDLED) deletes every `website-fraud/` object named in `payloadJson.fields.evidenceKeys` first (`deleteFileChecked`; the row survives while any object does) — the two new PII tables are outside the hand-maintained careers retention sweep, so their purge ships with them — and a SEPARATE orphan sweep removes any `website-fraud/` object older than 7 days (`WEBSITE_FRAUD_ORPHAN_AGE_MS`) that no FRAUD_REPORT row's `evidenceKeys` references at all (an upload the visitor never followed with a form submission), read via one query over every fraud row including test rows. Every threshold is a constant in `website-alarms.logic.ts`, code